{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2437 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "f5c401bd72bd0cab95538691483cff9afd8da37ef79af4f834b9b72cbe8cf9a2" :edb/db-before-t 2436 :edb/db-after-t 2437 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535749 50 #inst "2026-10-09T06:31:28.128Z" 13194139535749 true] [17592186171994 1020 #edb/ref 17592186364758 13194139535749 true] [17592186171995 1020 #edb/ref 17592186364730 13194139535749 true] [17592186171995 1020 #edb/ref 17592186364737 13194139535749 true] [17592186171996 1020 #edb/ref 17592186364744 13194139535749 true] [17592186171996 1020 #edb/ref 17592186364751 13194139535749 true] [17592186364730 1017 #edb/ref 17592186364731 13194139535749 true] [17592186364730 1089 "q-109713" 13194139535749 true] [17592186364730 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535749 true] [17592186364730 1100 "Find the equation of the tangent plane to the surface generated by the vector-valued function $r(u,v)=⟨2u+v,\\,{v}^{2}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡u,\\,uv⟩$ at the point where $u=0$ and $v=2.$" 13194139535749 true] [17592186364730 1113 #uuid "18388a52-c34d-5096-91df-d66aad50a515" 13194139535749 true] [17592186364730 1145 "We first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({v}^{2}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(uv)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡u,\\,v⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({v}^{2}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(uv)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,2v,\\,u⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate these vectors when $u=0$ and $v=2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(0,2) & =⟨2,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0),\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,1,\\,2⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(0,2) & =⟨1,\\,2(2),\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,4,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the surface is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={r}_{u}^{′}(0,2)\\times {r}_{v}^{′}(0,2) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-8,\\,2,\\,7⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the parameters $u=0$ and $v=2$ correspond to the point \n\n$$\n(2(0)+2,\\,{2}^{2}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡0,\\,0\\cdot 2)=(2,4,0),\n$$\n\nthe equation of the tangent plane is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨-8,\\,2,\\,7⟩\\cdot ⟨x-2,\\,y-4,\\,z⟩ & =0 \\\\ (-8)\\cdot (x-2)+2\\cdot (y-4)+7\\cdot z & =0 \\\\ -8x+2y+7z+8 & =0 \\\\ 8x-2y-7z & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535749 true] [17592186364731 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364732 13194139535749 true] [17592186364731 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364733 13194139535749 true] [17592186364731 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364734 13194139535749 true] [17592186364731 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364735 13194139535749 true] [17592186364731 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364736 13194139535749 true] [17592186364731 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535749 true] [17592186364731 1041 "selection" 13194139535749 true] [17592186364731 1104 #edb/ref 17592186364734 13194139535749 true] [17592186364731 1110 #uuid "3f2058d6-9b0c-565a-9822-120458ac4d00" 13194139535749 true] [17592186364732 1034 "x-y-z=1" 13194139535749 true] [17592186364732 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535749 true] [17592186364732 1111 #uuid "2c28204d-80b4-5bff-b6e8-3477b92e218b" 13194139535749 true] [17592186364733 1034 "4x-y-6z=2" 13194139535749 true] [17592186364733 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535749 true] [17592186364733 1111 #uuid "717424c2-ec13-5ac7-875e-88621ff7bdaf" 13194139535749 true] [17592186364734 1034 "8x-2y-7z=8" 13194139535749 true] [17592186364734 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535749 true] [17592186364734 1111 #uuid "2b8df72d-3c04-5e05-8795-e4c6fbaba38f" 13194139535749 true] [17592186364735 1034 "8x-y+2z=6" 13194139535749 true] [17592186364735 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535749 true] [17592186364735 1111 #uuid "95f9c3db-4482-5ce3-9b21-2d58e2f41fb8" 13194139535749 true] [17592186364736 1034 "2x-8y+3z=4" 13194139535749 true] [17592186364736 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535749 true] [17592186364736 1111 #uuid "da7a8a85-618c-5fdd-9471-3999ed61c8aa" 13194139535749 true] [17592186364737 1017 #edb/ref 17592186364738 13194139535749 true] [17592186364737 1089 "q-109764" 13194139535749 true] [17592186364737 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535749 true] [17592186364737 1100 "Find the equation of the tangent plane to the surface generated by the vector-valued function $r(u,v)=⟨2\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡v⟩$ at the point where $u=\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ and $v=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$" 13194139535749 true] [17592186364737 1113 #uuid "7b642b9a-3339-58d2-82e7-7f92410bd771" 13194139535749 true] [17592186364737 1145 "We first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(u,v) & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate these vectors when $u=\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ and $v=\\frac{\\pi }{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{3},\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =⟨-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}),\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}),\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\sqrt{3},\\,1,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{3},\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =⟨2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}),\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}),\\,-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,0,\\,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the surface is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={r}_{u}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{3},\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\times {r}_{v}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{3},\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -\\sqrt{3} & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{3} & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,-2\\sqrt{3},\\,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the parameters $u=\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ and $v=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ correspond to the point \n\n$$\n(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}),\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}),\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}))=(1,\\sqrt{3},0),\n$$\n\nthe equation of the tangent plane is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨-2,\\,-2\\sqrt{3},\\,0⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-\\sqrt{3},\\,z⟩ & =0 \\\\ (-2)\\cdot (x-1)-2\\sqrt{3}\\cdot (y-\\sqrt{3})+0\\cdot z & =0 \\\\ -2x-2\\sqrt{3\\,}y+8 & =0 \\\\ -x-\\sqrt{3}\\,y+4 & =0 \\\\ x+\\sqrt{3}\\,y & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535749 true] [17592186364738 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364739 13194139535749 true] [17592186364738 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364740 13194139535749 true] [17592186364738 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364741 13194139535749 true] [17592186364738 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364742 13194139535749 true] [17592186364738 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364743 131